= Positional bias (language model) =

== Overview ==
'''Positional bias''' in language models is systematic variation in model behavior caused by where otherwise comparable information or answer options occur in the input or output structure.

== Forms ==
Observed forms include preference for early options, late options, particular labels, or favorable locations within long contexts.

== Phenomenon versus mechanism ==
Position bias is a behavioral description. Different architectures, training procedures, prompt formats, and decoding setups can produce similar positional patterns.

== Measurement ==
Robust evaluation permutes option and evidence order while preserving semantics. A single ordering cannot establish positional bias.

